  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Cohesive dark command-center aesthetic, disciplined cyan/red/yellow semantics, strong headline presence, and polished cards/gauge. However, desktop composition is noticeably unbalanced: the oversized headline creates awkward wrapping while a large upper-right void remains. Tablet and mobile become very long and dense, with small low-contrast supporting text and cramped ledger values; the mobile header also truncates “Live Wire.” The hierarchy is clear, but responsive refinement and readability fall short of genuinely demo-ready polish.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero into a deliberate two-column composition, reduce headline size/line breaks, increase secondary-text contrast and minimum type size, give mobile ledger values more breathing room, and refine the compact header so labels do not appear accidentally clipped.",
